---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms | Ruby Smythe"
  description="Terms for using this site and for booking tattoo work, paintings, or commissions with Ruby Smythe."
>
  <main class="legal">
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated 13 September 2026</p>

    <h2>The site</h2>
    <p>
      This site shows my tattoo, painting, and drawing work. I try to keep it
      accurate, but images can flatter a piece. Colours shift from screen to
      screen, and a healed tattoo always settles differently from a fresh one.
      Nothing here is a quote, a price, or a promise of availability.
    </p>

    <h2>Copyright</h2>
    <p>
      Every artwork, drawing, and photograph on this site is my copyright, all
      rights reserved. Share links to the site as much as you like. You may not
      copy, repost, print, or sell the images, or feed them to AI models,
      without written permission from me.
    </p>
    <p>
      I also keep copyright in my tattoo designs. Paying for a tattoo does not
      transfer the design or give you the right to reproduce it.
    </p>

    <h2>Bookings and commissions</h2>
    <p>
      Bookings and commissions run through Instagram at
      <a
        href="https://www.instagram.com/byrubydesigns"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">@byrubydesigns</a
      >. Prices, deposits, and cancellation terms are confirmed in writing in
      that conversation before your appointment. A quote for one piece does not
      carry over to another.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      I do my best to keep this site online and correct, but I provide it as is,
      without warranties. I am not liable for losses that come from relying on
      it or from it being unavailable. Nothing in these terms limits your
      rights under consumer law.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms follow the law of Scotland, and any dispute belongs to the
      Scottish courts.
    </p>

    <p class="legal-back"><a href="/">Back to the portfolio</a></p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
